WEBVTT

00:02.211 --> 00:05.005
The resurrected companions

00:05.088 --> 00:07.883
were reunited with Fushi.

00:12.137 --> 00:13.305
And then...

00:13.889 --> 00:18.519
We're able to gather here like this
because our hearts are connected!

00:24.900 --> 00:27.611
Aoki, Mizuha is missing.

00:27.694 --> 00:29.613
She's been gone
since the day before yesterday...

01:58.118 --> 01:59.912
(To Your Eternity Season 3)

01:59.995 --> 02:03.999
(Episode 3 Mizuha)

02:12.841 --> 02:14.301
He's gone.

02:19.014 --> 02:20.891
President Hanna!

02:21.892 --> 02:23.727
We finally found you.

02:23.810 --> 02:25.854
President, are you okay?

02:28.857 --> 02:30.400
I'm fine.

02:30.484 --> 02:33.111
We'll also help you look
for Mizuha-senpai.

02:33.195 --> 02:36.657
The Vice Principal and others
went to town to look.

02:36.740 --> 02:40.536
Then let's split up
and search around here.

02:41.161 --> 02:44.873
I remember seeing
Mizuha-senpai here two days ago.

02:44.957 --> 02:48.919
And she went this way.

02:49.962 --> 02:52.756
Where did she go?

02:59.847 --> 03:02.891
Ouch!

03:08.605 --> 03:11.650
Cool! A wound as cool as Mr. Kai's.

03:12.109 --> 03:13.527
Yuki, what are you doing?

03:13.610 --> 03:15.612
Fushi, what are you doing here?

03:15.696 --> 03:17.906
I felt several sensations of pain.

03:17.990 --> 03:19.992
One of them is coming from you.

03:20.075 --> 03:22.703
You can even feel that? Amazing!

03:22.786 --> 03:25.163
Kazumitsu and Aiko are worried about you.

03:25.247 --> 03:26.164
Come on, let's go home.

03:26.248 --> 03:29.376
Wait, Mizuha-senpai is missing.

03:29.459 --> 03:31.253
I've been looking for her.

03:31.336 --> 03:32.254
Mizuha?

03:35.465 --> 03:37.551
I remember her leg was hurt.

03:38.302 --> 03:40.179
I think I know where that pain is.

03:40.262 --> 03:42.139
Really? That's amazing.

03:42.222 --> 03:43.515
I just need to make sure she's safe,

03:43.599 --> 03:45.392
and then send her home, right?

03:45.893 --> 03:47.102
I'll try.

03:47.394 --> 03:52.399
Mizuha! Mizuha!

03:52.482 --> 03:55.277
She must be troubled.

03:58.238 --> 04:01.116
I hope she doesn't do anything silly.

04:14.838 --> 04:16.590
President Hanna!

04:16.673 --> 04:18.717
The Vice Principal told me what happened.

04:18.800 --> 04:19.968
You'll catch a cold like this.

04:20.052 --> 04:22.429
Get in. We'll drive around and look.

04:22.513 --> 04:23.889
Okay.

04:25.015 --> 04:26.016
Are you okay?

04:26.099 --> 04:28.602
You should go home.

04:28.685 --> 04:30.020
I'm fine.

04:30.103 --> 04:32.689
I'm more worried about Mizuha's safety.

04:35.275 --> 04:36.902
Who are you?

04:42.866 --> 04:45.118
It hurts.

04:45.202 --> 04:48.622
I'm still not used to wearing high heels.

04:48.705 --> 04:50.457
Who are you? What are you doing here?

04:50.541 --> 04:52.084
I'm sorry. I'm Poco...

04:52.167 --> 04:54.378
I'm that Yuki-something's older sister.

04:54.461 --> 04:56.755
No, his cousin. From his mom's side.

04:56.839 --> 04:59.424
Yuki's cousin... Why are you here?

04:59.508 --> 05:02.386
He asked me to help you.

05:02.469 --> 05:04.054
Everyone is very worried about you.

05:04.137 --> 05:05.973
Come on, let's run away.

05:06.056 --> 05:09.017
Mizuha, is that your friend?

05:09.101 --> 05:11.687
You should've told me earlier.
I would've served tea.

05:11.770 --> 05:14.022
Grandpa, it's okay.

05:14.106 --> 05:17.776
- I'm going home.
- So this is your grandpa's house.

05:18.193 --> 05:20.070
Don't force yourself.

05:20.445 --> 05:21.738
If you don't want to stay at home,

05:21.822 --> 05:23.448
you're welcome to come anytime.

05:23.949 --> 05:24.992
Thank you, Grandpa.

05:26.577 --> 05:28.495
Big sister, let's go.

05:37.462 --> 05:38.505
Mizuha.

05:41.550 --> 05:43.969
Senpai, I was so worried about you.

05:44.052 --> 05:45.804
Are you hurt?

05:45.888 --> 05:48.390
Sorry, I'm fine.

05:48.765 --> 05:51.894
I'm so glad you're all right.

05:53.520 --> 05:54.354
I'm sorry.

05:55.230 --> 05:58.025
Could you be Fushi...

06:01.361 --> 06:04.114
Mizuha, what exactly are you up to?

06:04.198 --> 06:05.365
Where did you go?

06:05.449 --> 06:06.783
I went to Grandpa's house.

06:07.242 --> 06:08.952
He took you by force, didn't he?

06:09.036 --> 06:10.913
I won't forgive him. This is kidnapping.

06:10.996 --> 06:11.872
I'm calling the police.

06:11.955 --> 06:13.207
Wait! You're wrong!

06:13.290 --> 06:14.833
I went to Grandpa's house on my own.

06:15.459 --> 06:18.378
You'd even take a day off from school
just to go see your grandpa?

06:19.004 --> 06:21.298
Did I do something to upset you?

06:21.715 --> 06:24.259
No. It's my fault.

06:24.343 --> 06:27.930
I hadn't seen Grandpa in a while,
so I was feeling a bit lonely.

06:28.013 --> 06:30.974
Did he say or do anything to you?

06:31.058 --> 06:34.478
No, he just showed me a book.

06:34.561 --> 06:35.729
A book?

06:38.148 --> 06:40.609
I don't know if you've noticed,

06:40.692 --> 06:42.903
but your grandpa and I don't get along.

06:43.654 --> 06:44.738
I can tell.

06:44.821 --> 06:48.200
Then don't do anything
that'll make me sad.

06:49.409 --> 06:50.619
I'm sorry.

06:51.203 --> 06:53.121
It's good that you know.

06:53.997 --> 06:56.875
Everyone, thank you for your help today.

06:56.959 --> 06:59.002
I'll thank you properly someday.

06:59.086 --> 07:02.965
I'm glad to know that Mizuha
has such good friends in the end.

07:03.549 --> 07:04.633
In the end...

07:05.634 --> 07:07.845
I'm moving.

07:09.054 --> 07:11.223
Look, this is our new home.

07:11.306 --> 07:14.184
I want to match these curtains
with the floor.

07:14.268 --> 07:15.102
What do you think?

07:16.061 --> 07:16.937
I think it's good.

07:17.020 --> 07:18.480
Mizuha, don't move.

07:18.564 --> 07:20.399
Let's take this month's photo.

07:31.243 --> 07:32.870
If you leave, Mizuha,

07:33.245 --> 07:34.705
I'll cry.

07:34.788 --> 07:35.831
Hanna.

07:39.793 --> 07:42.337
If there's anything you want to say,
just say it.

07:42.421 --> 07:45.674
Don't hold back.
I'm willing to accept everything.

07:46.508 --> 07:47.718
I want to...

07:49.344 --> 07:51.013
stay here.

07:59.688 --> 08:01.607
Have you heard?

08:01.690 --> 08:02.900
Mizuha from Class 1.

08:02.983 --> 08:04.943
I heard she ran away from home.

08:05.569 --> 08:07.738
Yes, I heard. She's really bold.

08:07.821 --> 08:10.991
It's usually the quiet ones
that are scariest when they snap.

08:11.074 --> 08:14.870
I saw her talking
to a foreigner the other day.

08:14.953 --> 08:16.371
Seriously?

08:18.290 --> 08:20.542
Mizuha, let's go to the club.

08:21.418 --> 08:22.586
Okay.

08:28.175 --> 08:30.260
That feather... I made that.

08:30.344 --> 08:31.386
So it was you.

08:31.470 --> 08:32.304
I'm sorry.

08:32.387 --> 08:34.681
I saw you left it in the club room,
so I used it to tie my hair.

08:34.765 --> 08:37.726
It's okay. I made it for you.

08:37.809 --> 08:39.061
I knew it.

08:39.144 --> 08:41.063
By the way, how's your leg?

08:41.146 --> 08:42.814
I can run now.

08:42.898 --> 08:45.067
Don't push yourself too hard.

08:46.401 --> 08:47.486
There you go again.

08:47.569 --> 08:50.614
We're not the Otaku Club
or the Occult Research Club.

08:52.199 --> 08:54.076
We're the Creative Literature Club.

08:54.618 --> 08:56.703
How's the moving going?

08:56.787 --> 08:57.996
I'm not sure yet.

08:58.080 --> 08:59.164
I see.

08:59.248 --> 09:01.625
Why don't you talk to your mom
about it again?

09:01.708 --> 09:03.001
Tell her you don't want to move.

09:03.544 --> 09:06.046
Good morning, my two senpai!

09:06.129 --> 09:08.549
Yuki, you scared me.

09:08.632 --> 09:09.883
It's not morning anymore.

09:09.967 --> 09:10.884
You're right.

09:10.968 --> 09:12.427
But that's the industry way.

09:12.719 --> 09:15.931
Mizuha, I'm sure it'll go well.

09:24.565 --> 09:29.236
Mizuha, I'm going to wash
this blouse and dress.

09:29.319 --> 09:31.613
Okay, Mom. Thank you.

09:38.704 --> 09:40.956
- Mom, I wanted to tell you...
- Mizuha, I'm sorry.

09:41.039 --> 09:45.669
As your mother, I should have
understood why you ran away.

09:45.752 --> 09:47.337
What upsets me the most is

09:47.421 --> 09:50.841
that Mizuha's heart is drifting
further and further from me.

09:50.924 --> 09:53.510
So I've decided not to move.

09:55.596 --> 09:57.139
Mom, thank you.

09:57.222 --> 09:58.390
I'm so happy.

10:07.274 --> 10:10.235
Mom, have you seen my feather hair tie?

10:10.319 --> 10:12.362
No. Did you look carefully?

10:12.446 --> 10:15.657
It's not in the laundry basket.
That's strange.

10:15.741 --> 10:17.826
I'm sure I left it on the sink.

10:17.910 --> 10:19.912
It can't be helped if you lost it.

10:20.204 --> 10:21.663
Give me your hand.

10:23.790 --> 10:24.917
This is...

10:25.000 --> 10:28.504
This is my favorite hair tie
from elementary school.

10:28.587 --> 10:32.716
I hoped that one day I could use it to tie
the hair of a child as cute as Mizuha,

10:32.799 --> 10:36.386
so I've been taking
really good care of it.

10:36.470 --> 10:38.430
Is it okay for you to give me
something so important?

10:38.514 --> 10:40.933
What if I lose it again?

10:41.016 --> 10:43.393
It's fine. Turn around.

10:48.941 --> 10:51.527
Look, it suits you very well.

10:53.445 --> 10:55.447
You're my precious girl.

10:59.284 --> 11:00.953
I'm really sorry!

11:01.245 --> 11:03.956
I lost the hair tie you gave me.

11:04.039 --> 11:05.415
Don't worry about it.

11:05.499 --> 11:07.334
It's nice to wear the same hair tie,

11:07.417 --> 11:10.671
but even if you lose it,
it won't break our bond.

11:10.754 --> 11:11.880
Hanna.

11:11.964 --> 11:14.174
Actually, I'm glad it's gone.

11:14.258 --> 11:18.887
Losing it made me realize
how much your mom cares about you.

11:19.346 --> 11:21.431
This hair tie really suits you.

11:21.515 --> 11:22.599
Really?

11:22.683 --> 11:24.643
And you don't have to move anymore.

11:25.561 --> 11:27.688
If I take you out now,

11:27.771 --> 11:28.856
your mom won't be mad, right?

11:28.939 --> 11:30.315
What do you mean?

11:30.399 --> 11:33.318
Let's go to the station mall this weekend.

11:33.402 --> 11:34.653
I want to buy a hand mirror.

11:36.446 --> 11:37.739
I'll ask Mom when I get home.

11:40.450 --> 11:42.661
It's cute. This is nice too.

11:47.749 --> 11:49.710
Okay, I'll buy this one.

11:50.335 --> 11:52.045
Thank you very much.

11:52.546 --> 11:55.299
It looks good on you.

11:57.885 --> 11:58.886
You got complimented!

12:01.013 --> 12:02.681
This one is cute.

12:02.764 --> 12:03.599
Which one?

12:03.682 --> 12:05.017
I think I'll buy this one.

12:07.186 --> 12:09.396
That's good. It really suits you.

12:11.815 --> 12:13.567
Let's buy this set of hairpins together.

12:13.650 --> 12:14.610
Sure.

12:14.693 --> 12:16.737
There's a new crepe shop
on the third floor.

12:16.820 --> 12:17.821
Have you been there?

12:17.905 --> 12:18.906
No.

12:19.448 --> 12:20.490
Let's go.

12:32.419 --> 12:35.464
Sure enough, eating two is really filling.

12:35.547 --> 12:37.508
Mom might scold me when I get home.

12:37.591 --> 12:38.759
You ate too much.

12:38.842 --> 12:40.802
I'm still growing.

12:41.637 --> 12:44.723
Life feels pretty peaceful, doesn't it?

12:50.771 --> 12:52.814
Wh-Why are you crying?

12:55.400 --> 12:57.819
Well... let's hang out again next time.

13:01.198 --> 13:02.115
I'm home.

13:02.199 --> 13:03.200
Welcome home.

13:03.283 --> 13:05.327
Mizuha, did you have fun?

13:06.703 --> 13:07.996
Yes, I did.

13:09.289 --> 13:10.791
Mizuha?

13:12.417 --> 13:14.753
(To Your Eternity Season 3)

13:15.671 --> 13:17.840
Many people around me

13:17.923 --> 13:20.259
thought I was perfect

13:20.342 --> 13:22.261
and had everything I needed.

13:23.136 --> 13:24.972
I thought so too.

13:25.806 --> 13:27.432
No matter what it was,

13:27.516 --> 13:29.852
I learned faster than others.

13:30.519 --> 13:32.312
Academics were no problem for me.

13:33.313 --> 13:36.692
Many people praised me in sports too.

13:37.776 --> 13:40.028
Then Mizuha will be in the middle.

13:40.112 --> 13:42.698
Why is it always her?

13:43.198 --> 13:44.867
This move is simple.

13:44.950 --> 13:46.743
Everyone should be able to do it.

13:49.580 --> 13:52.332
Why can't you do something so simple?

13:52.666 --> 13:54.668
I thought I was perfect.

13:54.751 --> 13:56.628
But when I entered junior high school,

13:56.712 --> 13:59.298
I realized there were things
I couldn't have too.

13:59.381 --> 14:01.925
Amazing. Mizuha, you write so well.

14:02.009 --> 14:03.427
Exactly.

14:03.510 --> 14:06.221
The first was a perfect friend.

14:06.305 --> 14:08.223
Do you want to go out with me?

14:08.307 --> 14:09.141
I'm sorry.

14:09.224 --> 14:11.768
I hate people who are inferior to me.

14:11.852 --> 14:15.647
There's no merit in being
with someone I can't respect.

14:16.315 --> 14:18.650
The second was a perfect mother.

14:18.734 --> 14:22.112
My mom's been making me learn
all sorts of things since I was little.

14:22.571 --> 14:24.615
I don't hate it.

14:24.698 --> 14:26.909
I can do anything anyway.

14:26.992 --> 14:29.244
Mom, look at the trophy.

14:30.287 --> 14:33.415
Mizuha, you're the reason I live.

14:33.498 --> 14:36.627
To Mom, I'm just a trophy.

14:37.336 --> 14:42.216
The third was time
that could only be used to please Mom.

14:42.674 --> 14:45.552
Eternal time, eternal youth.

14:45.636 --> 14:48.013
No matter how hard I try,

14:48.096 --> 14:50.682
wrinkles will still appear around my eyes.

14:50.766 --> 14:52.226
It's ugly.

14:52.309 --> 14:54.561
I'm perfect because I'm young.

14:54.645 --> 14:56.688
Once I get old,
I'll be just an ordinary person.

14:58.106 --> 14:59.650
I want to die.

15:00.067 --> 15:01.735
Before I knew it,

15:01.818 --> 15:06.365
I started dreaming of ending my life
before I became an adult.

15:07.157 --> 15:10.118
I know this personality isn't good.

15:10.494 --> 15:13.038
But I truly can't change.

15:13.121 --> 15:18.085
If only someone could truly
snap me out of it one day.

15:18.168 --> 15:20.754
Hanna, you should be careful too.

15:20.838 --> 15:23.257
Actually, she likes
messing around with boys.

15:23.340 --> 15:24.424
No way!

15:24.508 --> 15:27.010
She's not that free.

15:28.345 --> 15:31.390
Don't worry.
There are people willing to catch me.

15:32.015 --> 15:35.310
People who'd accept
even someone as hated as me.

15:37.646 --> 15:39.773
If I died,

15:40.148 --> 15:41.400
would you cry for me?

15:44.152 --> 15:47.030
I thought she'd catch me.

15:47.114 --> 15:49.074
But she didn't answer right away.

15:49.449 --> 15:51.577
That broke my heart.

15:52.619 --> 15:55.205
Don't neglect your injury.

16:00.502 --> 16:04.423
When you grow up,
you'll face more obstacles.

16:04.506 --> 16:08.385
Work, family, relationships, pride.

16:09.094 --> 16:13.098
I'll probably die around 17.

16:14.099 --> 16:16.894
We're moving next month, so be ready.

16:18.687 --> 16:20.689
I said we're moving.

16:23.400 --> 16:27.905
I already told Dad not to send
any more letters.

16:30.782 --> 16:32.492
Regret.

16:33.785 --> 16:35.621
I can't quite describe it,

16:35.704 --> 16:38.332
but something still lingers in my heart.

16:38.415 --> 16:42.211
Honestly, I really don't know
what Mom is thinking.

16:42.294 --> 16:45.881
Am I still not perfect enough for Mom?

16:46.965 --> 16:48.634
I rebelled a little,

16:49.259 --> 16:51.094
treating it like a game.

16:58.936 --> 17:01.647
Mizuha, why are you here?

17:02.356 --> 17:04.024
Have you told your mom?

17:04.107 --> 17:05.359
Yes...

17:06.318 --> 17:10.739
I see. Then your mom
must be willing to accept it.

17:11.615 --> 17:15.494
I mean, to hand over
the Guardian Force to Mizuha.

17:15.953 --> 17:18.455
What is the Guardian Force?

17:18.539 --> 17:20.624
For generations, our family

17:20.707 --> 17:23.418
has been involved
in what you'd call religious activities.

17:26.046 --> 17:28.257
In this shabby house?

17:28.757 --> 17:31.802
You must be wondering
where the believers are, right?

17:31.885 --> 17:35.013
Because someone doesn't allow us
to preach openly,

17:35.097 --> 17:38.308
the believers don't engage
in missionary work.

17:38.684 --> 17:42.729
You'll be the 18th generation,
the current head of the group.

17:43.105 --> 17:47.901
But your mother refused,
so she cut ties with me.

17:48.777 --> 17:50.362
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

17:50.445 --> 17:53.574
Actually, I came here today
without telling Mom.

17:53.657 --> 17:56.118
She's probably busy looking
for me right now.

17:57.286 --> 17:58.579
You seem to be having fun.

17:58.662 --> 18:00.831
I'd like to know more
about what you said just now.

18:00.914 --> 18:02.916
What is this Guardian Force protecting?

18:03.876 --> 18:06.295
An immortal monster.

18:06.920 --> 18:09.590
The study still holds
all the records up to now.

18:09.673 --> 18:11.300
You can take a look.

18:17.723 --> 18:20.893
My ancestor was a woman named Hayase.

18:20.976 --> 18:23.979
It all started
when she protected that monster.

18:24.396 --> 18:26.690
The monster could bring
people around him back to life

18:26.773 --> 18:28.150
and make them his allies.

18:28.567 --> 18:31.111
At that time,
he saved the ancient capital Renril

18:31.195 --> 18:35.199
from the threat of the legendary creatures
known as the Nokkers.

18:35.866 --> 18:38.118
That monster's name was Fushi.

18:40.537 --> 18:42.539
It's just a legend.

18:47.085 --> 18:48.337
Listen, everyone!

18:48.420 --> 18:50.589
I found Beast Boy!

18:50.672 --> 18:52.341
Of course, he's family.

18:52.424 --> 18:54.843
My grandpa and sister love Fushi.

19:03.018 --> 19:04.520
Everyone is very worried about you.

19:05.103 --> 19:09.900
No one can get in through
the only ventilation window in this room.

19:10.734 --> 19:14.696
My small act of rebellion
led me to a great discovery.

19:15.364 --> 19:16.698
The missing piece of my puzzle.

19:16.782 --> 19:18.659
What I truly need.

19:19.034 --> 19:21.662
Instead of lamenting over what I lack,

19:21.745 --> 19:25.707
I'd rather have something
that surpasses everything.

19:25.791 --> 19:28.710
That way, I can reach perfection
for the first time in my life.

19:29.586 --> 19:31.004
I...

19:31.839 --> 19:33.507
want...

19:34.675 --> 19:36.134
him.

19:40.389 --> 19:41.932
It's strange.

19:42.015 --> 19:45.018
I've never felt happiness
like this before.

19:45.102 --> 19:47.271
Is it possible
that when we have a greater goal,

19:47.354 --> 19:52.109
all negative emotions
will become insignificant?

19:54.444 --> 19:58.031
My hair tie really suits you.

19:58.115 --> 20:01.118
An imperfect mom isn't half bad either.

20:01.910 --> 20:03.161
Mizuha-senpai!

20:03.245 --> 20:05.330
That hair accessory is really pretty.

20:05.414 --> 20:07.916
Really? It's my mom's treasure.

20:08.000 --> 20:09.418
So... So cute!

20:10.085 --> 20:11.211
I'm glad.

20:11.670 --> 20:14.715
An imperfect friend isn't half bad either.

20:15.591 --> 20:19.511
Those fleeting, chaotic days
aren't half bad either.

20:20.429 --> 20:22.723
If something is lacking, I'll create it.

20:22.806 --> 20:24.808
I'll try to connect the dots.

20:25.184 --> 20:32.191
How perfect can my life be
with my own hands?

20:37.863 --> 20:39.907
Bye, Mizuha.

20:55.380 --> 20:56.715
That's strange.

20:57.049 --> 20:58.884
When did I get home?

20:59.301 --> 21:02.387
Did I fall asleep in the hallway?

21:09.269 --> 21:10.103
Dad?

21:10.187 --> 21:12.606
Mizuha, I'm spending the night
at my parents' house today.

21:12.689 --> 21:14.066
You can eat first.

21:14.149 --> 21:15.234
Okay.

21:15.317 --> 21:17.110
How's Auntie's leg?

21:17.194 --> 21:19.404
It's fine. She's asleep now.

21:19.488 --> 21:21.073
Please tell Mom for me.

21:21.657 --> 21:22.783
Bye.

21:22.866 --> 21:26.245
Mom, Dad said he's not coming home today.

21:31.750 --> 21:33.001
Mom!

21:35.045 --> 21:36.630
Mom!

21:43.554 --> 21:46.014
M-Mom.

22:07.119 --> 22:08.912
What happened?

22:08.996 --> 22:10.163
Mom.

22:11.123 --> 22:13.834
Why am I running away?

22:13.917 --> 22:16.128
I can't remember anything.

22:17.254 --> 22:18.338
Dad.

22:19.006 --> 22:20.465
I need to contact Dad...

22:20.549 --> 22:21.925
What's that?

22:22.009 --> 22:23.594
Gosh, don't look.

22:24.970 --> 22:26.180
Let's go after it.

22:26.263 --> 22:27.097
Are you filming this?

22:27.181 --> 22:29.516
Stop it. Let's go.

22:30.475 --> 22:32.394
Did I kill her?

22:32.895 --> 22:35.689
Someone, please help me.

22:35.772 --> 22:39.902
Couldn't you ask
your favorite friend for help

22:41.695 --> 22:43.405
before things turned out this way?

22:44.156 --> 22:48.285
Is there anything I can do for you?

22:50.996 --> 22:52.789
Be...

22:53.665 --> 22:56.043
my friend.

24:29.970 --> 24:31.722
(Next Episode Preview)

24:31.805 --> 24:34.808
A town so peaceful, it's boring.

24:35.392 --> 24:40.355
In a dark corner,
the young girl killed her mother.

24:41.690 --> 24:44.234
Under the watchful eyes
of those around them,

24:44.651 --> 24:47.779
Fushi and Mizuha grow closer.

24:48.363 --> 24:52.910
And then, something strange happens.

24:52.993 --> 24:54.995
(Episode 4 The Deceased)
